WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.164 --> 00:00:02.416
- Product name, Mango Creamy Soda,

00:00:02.416 --> 00:00:04.587
parentheses, carbonated drink.

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:08.370
(pouring liquid sound)

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.155
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.155 --> 00:00:13.214
- Peering down the bottle
at what color this is

00:00:13.214 --> 00:00:15.572
I'm like a little suspect of it.

00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:17.722
- Look at the milky white.

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:18.763
- Little cloudy.

00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:20.342
- Can we say the thing
we think it looks like?

00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:22.223
- It looks like (bleep).

00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:23.941
- Good luck.

00:00:23.941 --> 00:00:25.230
- It tastes like mango juice.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.111
- It tastes just like a bunch of

00:00:27.111 --> 00:00:30.907
melted Haribo gummies in dirty water.

00:00:30.907 --> 00:00:33.468
- I would 100% drink this soda.

00:00:35.203 --> 00:00:36.863
- I would definitely buy this at the store

00:00:36.863 --> 00:00:39.533
because it's so tiny and I would love

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:42.169
to just carry it around
and have people comment.

00:00:42.169 --> 00:00:43.585
(lid pops)
- Oh, cool!

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:45.582
- Oh my God!
- (screams) What?

00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:46.983
- What a surprise.

00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:49.578
- Oh, it packs a punch.
- It's like liquid Smarties.

00:00:49.578 --> 00:00:51.294
- It does like a little bit of Red Bull.

00:00:51.294 --> 00:00:53.047
- It's an entirely new taste to me.

00:00:53.047 --> 00:00:55.612
- I like it.

00:00:55.612 --> 00:00:56.732
- It's okay.

00:00:56.732 --> 00:00:57.607
(laughing)

00:00:59.131 --> 00:01:02.184
- Cool, I see Hello Kitty
and I know Hello Kitty.

00:01:02.184 --> 00:01:03.520
- There's a paragraph of instructions

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.893
on how to open it.
- There's some down here too.

00:01:04.893 --> 00:01:06.535
- Oh, this punches.
(cracking)

00:01:06.535 --> 00:01:08.779
- Place opener on top of a Ramune bottle

00:01:08.779 --> 00:01:10.785
and press down firmly with your palm.

00:01:12.584 --> 00:01:13.815
(cracking)

00:01:13.815 --> 00:01:15.140
- Oh my God!

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.458
- Am I doing it right?

00:01:16.458 --> 00:01:18.878
At this point, lunch is
over, my lunch break is over.

00:01:20.724 --> 00:01:22.502
- Alright, that's not bad.

00:01:22.502 --> 00:01:24.418
- It's super sugary.

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:25.550
(sound of disgust)

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.035
- Yeah, that's the worst one yet.

00:01:27.035 --> 00:01:27.845
- Really?

00:01:27.845 --> 00:01:29.967
- I really like it, actually
it reminds me of the

00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:31.712
frozen ice pops.

00:01:31.712 --> 00:01:33.798
- This tastes like Jones Soda to me.

00:01:33.798 --> 00:01:34.894
- I would agree with that.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.306
- I think, like, mixing this with alcohol

00:01:36.306 --> 00:01:37.885
at a party would be fun.

00:01:37.885 --> 00:01:39.801
- I noticed you just poured more of this.

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.345
You went back for seconds.

00:01:41.345 --> 00:01:43.644
- I think there's a chemical in this

00:01:43.644 --> 00:01:47.326
that's controlling my brain more than me.

00:01:48.315 --> 00:01:49.338
(lid popping)

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:55.695
- What is that?

00:01:55.695 --> 00:01:57.111
- It kinda smells like rotting fruit.

00:01:57.111 --> 00:01:58.864
- What does that smell like?

00:01:58.864 --> 00:02:00.977
- (laughing) What is that smell?

00:02:00.977 --> 00:02:02.307
- This soda's angry at me.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.785
- Nope, nope.
(laughing)

00:02:04.785 --> 00:02:06.167
I'm against this taste.

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:09.068
- Oh goddammit.
- Wow, that's very unpleasant.

00:02:09.068 --> 00:02:12.531
- Kind of a sour,
(snapping) sparkling cider.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:14.964
- Yeah, this makes my
tongue wanna leave my mouth.

00:02:14.964 --> 00:02:15.772
- Yeah.

00:02:15.772 --> 00:02:18.009
- Like apple puree for babies.
- Yes!

00:02:18.009 --> 00:02:19.909
That's exactly what it is!
- It's like a baby food.

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:21.148
- It's baby food soda.

00:02:21.148 --> 00:02:24.737
- [Voiceover] I have arrived,
I shall take one tiny beer.

00:02:25.721 --> 00:02:29.060
- Are you enjoying the
giant football game?

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.895
Throw me one of that tiny six-pack.

00:02:31.895 --> 00:02:34.066
- Here, one tiny beer for you.

00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:37.128
- One tiny beer.
(laughs)

